post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
The session is installed, but not yet the greeter default. To preselect it in
gtkgreet (rewrites only the -c argument of /etc/greetd/config.toml, with
timestamped backups, and adds it to /etc/greetd/environments):

  sudo cosmic-comp-traffic-session-default

That takes effect at the next greetd start: a reboot, or
`systemctl restart greetd` while logged out. Until then the session is still
selectable from the greeter's session list.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
If this session is the greeter default, point /etc/greetd/config.toml at another
command first, otherwise the greeter will try to log into a missing session:

  sudo cp -a /etc/greetd/config.toml.bak.<timestamp> /etc/greetd/config.toml
EOF
}
